title: MikroTik REST API: Filesystem system disk
agents: mikrotik_rest_api
catalog: hw/network/mikrotik
license: GPL
distribution: check_mk
description:
 Usage of the system storage of a MikroTik RouterOS device
 ({total-hdd-space} and {free-hdd-space} of {/system/resource}), with
 the standard filesystem check: levels, magic factor and trends via the
 rule {File systems (used space and growth)}, default WARN at 80%,
 CRIT at 90%. Bad blocks of the NAND flash are only shown in the
 details, they have their own service {NAND bad blocks}.

 On a host that is also polled via SNMP this service takes precedence:
 the agent section supersedes the SNMP section (hr_fs), so the
 service is never created twice.

 To connect to the MikroTik device a special datasource program is
 used: {MikroTik RouterOS (mikrotik-rest-api)} in Setup > Agents >
 Other integrations, module "RouterOS Info, CPU, memory, system disk,
 uptime".

 Added in mikrotik-rest-api 1.0.0 by Klaus Paulitsch.

perfdata:
 Used, free and total space, growth and trend.

inventory:
 One service, item {system disk}.
